6. Scope, limits and signed handoff

OwnedChild still exclusively owns the private Child and registration. Every
wait and Drop fences the group before reap. SIGCHLD autoreaping is refused;
the MCP SDK receives only byte pipes. Foreign unsafe waitpid on another
owner's child, or installing autoreaping after spawn, violates the explicit
ownership precondition. ECHILD cannot retrospectively repair that external
reap. Pinned Tokio 1.54.1 sees this child in its orphan queue only after our
Drop fence. These are the unchanged, reviewed assumptions.
Foreign-pgid reuse is deterministic injection after a real leader release,
using the fixture's own group, rather than forcing Darwin's allocator to wrap.
Finite-model parity does not prove arbitrary Rust refinement; OS/SC/signal
instructions have implementation witnesses. Wall-clock benchmarks stay outside
the canonical gate. No live-provider smoke was assigned or added. No real
credential value was printed or committed. No assigned finding is waived.

